{
  "imnb_version": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Raag Khamaj Tutorial + Sitar Composition - Saptak Music School"
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Raag Khamaj Masterclass",
        "",
        "**Thaat**: Khamaj  ",
        "**Vadi**: Ga  ",
        "**Samvadi**: Ni  ",
        "**Time**: 2nd Prahar of Night (roughly 9:00 PM – 12:00 AM)",
        "",
        "Khamaj is a popular raga known for its romantic and light classical nature (Thumri style). It uses **Shuddha Ni** in Aroha (Ascent) and **Komal Ni** in Avroha (Descent). All other notes are Shuddha.",
        "",
        "This notebook demonstrates all features of the **sargam-v1** language while teaching Raag Khamaj."
      ],
      "id": "68ffc214-7a28-4a6e-aefa-70ed9777d5d3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 1. Basic Scale: Aroha & Avroha",
        "",
        "**Aroha**: ",
        "  - Uses Shuddha Ni (N).",
        "  - Banned note: Re",
        "",
        "**Descent**: ",
        "  - Uses Komal Ni (n).",
        "",
        "### Scale Structure:",
        "",
        "**Aroha**: Sa - Ga - Ma - Pa - Dha - Ni - Sa'",
        "",
        "**Avroha**: Sa' - Ni (komal) - Dha - Pa - Ma - Ga - Re - Sa"
      ],
      "id": "5242f2f8-6763-4dd4-8241-86fb38843246"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@raga Khamaj",
        "",
        "# Aroha (Ascent)",
        "S G M P D N S' ||",
        "",
        "# Avroha (Descent)",
        "S' n D P M G R S ||"
      ],
      "id": "14cab560-c67c-47a5-bfd7-c44d3aec130e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 2. Composition",
        "",
        "This section presents a Vilambit (slow tempo) composition set to the 16-beat rhythmic cycle known as Teentaal. ",
        "",
        "The melody allows for a detailed exploration of the raga's romantic temperament. "
      ],
      "id": "3f689a5b-9978-4e7c-b710-b3fcda638e1b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tala Tintal(16)",
        "@tala_pattern dha dhin dhin dha | dha dhin dhin dha | dha tin tin ta | ta dhin dhin dha",
        "@tempo 50",
        "",
        "## Gat / Sthayi / Line 1",
        "",
        ".:4 | .:4 | .3  S:0.5 S:0.5 | G:0.5 ^:0.5 m:0.5 m:0.5 P:0.5 D:0.25 D:0.25 N:0.5 S':0.5 |",
        "N:0.5 ^:0.5 N:0.5 ^:0.5 S':0.5 ^:0.5 n:0.5 n:0.5 | D:0.5 ^:0.5 m:0.5 m:0.5 P:0.5 ^:0.5 D:0.5 ^:0.5 | G:0.5 ^:0.5 m:0.5 ^:0.5 G:0.5 ^:0.5",
        "",
        "# Line 2",
        ".:11 S:0.5 S:0.5 n,:0.5 ^:0.5 S:0.5 S:0.5 m:0.5 ^:0.5 G:0.5 ^:0.5 |",
        "S:0.5 ^:0.5 n,:0.5 ^:0.5 D,:0.5 ^:0.5 P,:0.5 D,:0.5 | N,:0.5 ^:0.5 S:0.5 S:0.5 G:0.5 m:0.25 m:0.25 P:0.5 D:0.5 | G:0.5 ^:0.5 m:0.5 ^:0.5 G:0.5 ^:0.5 |",
        ""
      ],
      "id": "7ce070fa-31a8-441a-b462-498403ae6453"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 3. Durations & Timing",
        "",
        "Control note durations with `:duration` syntax:",
        "- `S:2` = Sa lasting 2 beats",
        "- `G:0.5` = Ga lasting half a beat (double speed)",
        "- `M:0.25` = Ma lasting quarter beat (quadruple speed)",
        "- `@default_duration 1` sets the default duration for notes without explicit duration"
      ],
      "id": "8077bb71-d8ce-43e9-a247-bd59f2da12a2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tempo 100",
        "",
        "# Different durations",
        "S:2 R:2 G:2 M:2 ||",
        "P:1 D:1 N:1 S':1 ||",
        "",
        "# Fast phrases (Taans)",
        "S:0.5 R:0.5 G:0.5 M:0.5 | P:0.5 D:0.5 N:0.5 S':0.5 ||",
        "",
        "# Very fast (Chhota Khayal style)",
        "S:0.25 R:0.25 G:0.25 M:0.25 | P:0.25 D:0.25 N:0.25 S':0.25 ||"
      ],
      "id": "1c784478-22ba-4bcc-a6de-71de4d6f1702"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 4. Rests & Holds",
        "",
        "- `_` = Rest (silence) - can have duration: `_0.5`",
        "- `.` = Hold (extends previous note) - can have duration: `.2`",
        "",
        "These are essential for creating rhythmic patterns and pauses."
      ],
      "id": "f2316366-0d98-41b9-bae5-556ddc8f67b3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tempo 100",
        "",
        "# Using rests and holds",
        "G M P D | _ . N S' | n D P M | G R S . ||",
        "",
        "# Rests with explicit duration",
        "S:1 _:1 G:1 _:1 | M:1 _:1 P:1 _:1 ||",
        "",
        "# Holds extending notes",
        "S . . . | R . G . | M . P . | D . N . ||"
      ],
      "id": "51e51985-5a6e-4f02-9c86-dec3c7c8d24a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 5. Tala & Bar Markers",
        "",
        "Talas define the rhythmic cycle:",
        "- `@tala Tintal(16)` = 16-beat cycle (4+4+4+4)",
        "- `@tala_pattern` = Specifies tabla bols (syllables) with timing (e.g., `dha dhin dhin dha`)",
        "- `|` = Vibhag divider (bar marker)",
        "- `||` = End of avartan (complete cycle)",
        "",
        "Common talas: Tintal (16), Teental (16), Jhaptal (10), Ektaal (12), Rupak (7)"
      ],
      "id": "00f61a18-c673-4709-a97a-07aeffc99ab6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tala Tintal(16)",
        "@tala_pattern dha dhin dhin dha | dha dhin dhin dha | dha tin tin ta | ta dhin dhin dha",
        "@tempo 100",
        "",
        "# Sthayi in Tintal (16 beats = 4 vibhags)",
        "G M P D | N S' S' . | n D P M | G R S . ||",
        "G M P D | N S' R' S' | n D P M | G R S . ||"
      ],
      "id": "2e12a52b-c952-4b81-8202-17fa81a4b9b5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tala Jhaptal(10)",
        "@tala_pattern dha dhin | dha dhin dhin | dha tin | ta dhin dhin",
        "@tempo 90",
        "",
        "# Composition in Jhaptal (10 beats = 2+3+2+3)",
        "G M:0.5 P:0.5 | D N:0.5 S':0.5 . | n D | P M G:0.5 R:0.5 ||"
      ],
      "id": "f3ddb106-5c6a-41cf-8ca9-b75217268ea0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 6. Ornamentation - Meend (Slides)",
        "",
        "Meend creates smooth glides between notes:",
        "- `S+meend(P)` = Slide from Sa to Pa over the note's duration",
        "- `G+meend(M, 0.2, 0.6, 0.2)` = Three-phase meend: play G for 0.2 beats, slide to M over 0.6 beats, hold M for 0.2 beats"
      ],
      "id": "59ee5152-c7e2-4bbf-a0f1-c42806e93b8b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tempo 80",
        "",
        "# Simple meend",
        "S+meend(P) . . . ||",
        "G+meend(M) . . . ||",
        "",
        "# Three-phase meend (more expressive)",
        "S+meend(P, 0.3, 0.4, 0.3) . . ||",
        "G+meend(M, 0.2, 0.6, 0.2) . . ||"
      ],
      "id": "ed495aea-4790-48b1-85a3-4e358e8e8af3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 7. Ornamentation - Kan (Grace Notes)",
        "",
        "Kan adds a quick grace note before the main note:",
        "- `G+kan(R)` = Quick grace note from R into G",
        "- Creates a subtle ornamentation typical in Khamaj"
      ],
      "id": "006826d7-081f-4e56-a418-1491769a3d1e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tempo 100",
        "",
        "# Kan ornamentation",
        "G+kan(R) M+kan(G) | P+kan(M) D+kan(P) ||",
        "",
        "# Kan with longer notes",
        "S+kan(N) . . . | G+kan(S) . . . ||"
      ],
      "id": "0d6b0b54-8a5b-43b3-9470-0fce73590e76"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 8. Ornamentation - Andolan & Kampita (Oscillations)",
        "",
        "- `+andolan(amount)` = Slow oscillation around the swara",
        "- `+kampita(speed)` = Fast oscillation (vibrato-like)",
        "- `+shake` = Rapid repeated alternation"
      ],
      "id": "89de0d49-06ba-49c8-9837-7649c7b7af50"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tempo 80",
        "",
        "# Andolan (slow oscillation)",
        "G+andolan(0.1) . . . | M+andolan(0.15) . . . ||",
        "",
        "# Kampita (fast oscillation)",
        "P+kampita(8) . . . | D+kampita(10) . . . ||",
        "",
        "# Shake (rapid alternation)",
        "N+shake . . . | S'+shake . . . ||"
      ],
      "id": "fe0b1e4e-d7f3-4027-99a7-e644d06cecb9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 9. Microtonal Notation (Shruti)",
        "",
        "Indian classical music uses microtones. Use `n+amountc` (cents) or `n+amountst` (semitones):",
        "- `Gn+25c` = Ga with +25 cents (slightly higher)",
        "- `Mn-15c` = Ma with -15 cents (slightly lower)",
        "- `n+0.25st` = +0.25 semitone offset"
      ],
      "id": "a3937e89-8d44-46af-b7c8-14803d2469d0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tempo 80",
        "",
        "# Microtonal variations",
        "Gn+20c . . . | Mn-10c . . . ||",
        "Pn+15c . . . | Dn+25c . . . ||",
        "",
        "# Subtle shruti adjustments",
        "Gn+12c Mn+8c | Pn+18c Dn+22c ||"
      ],
      "id": "4ac1956d-fc7d-48ad-a5b3-f19a9049b0b8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 10. Lyrics",
        "",
        "Associate lyrics with notes using `=\"lyric\"` syntax:",
        "- `G=\"mo\"` = Ga with lyric \"mo\"",
        "- Useful for bandish, thumri, and vocal compositions"
      ],
      "id": "11bf418e-a6e1-4fa2-bff4-452e53add840"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tempo 100",
        "",
        "# Simple bandish phrase with lyrics",
        "G=\"mo\" M=\"han\" | P=\"se\" D=\"na\" | N=\"a\" S'=\"a\" . ||",
        "",
        "# Longer phrase",
        "S=\"ra\" G=\"ga\" M=\"kha\" | P=\"ma\" D=\"ja\" N=\"me\" S'=\"in\" ||"
      ],
      "id": "da24f778-f9f9-48ab-a446-f41b40cbbde9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 11. Polyphony - Multiple Voices",
        "",
        "Create multiple simultaneous parts using `#voice` declarations:",
        "- Each voice plays independently",
        "- Common use: melody + tanpura drone",
        "- Can have any number of voices"
      ],
      "id": "6b423385-509f-47ae-8982-64077dd8fe26"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tempo 120",
        "",
        "#voice melody",
        "G . M . | P . D . | N S' n D | P M G R ||",
        "",
        "#voice tanpura",
        "S,, . . . | P,, . . . | S,, . . . | P,, . . . ||"
      ],
      "id": "e6f683d3-1c73-41b7-9cae-22eaad9417e4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tempo 100",
        "",
        "#voice main",
        "G M P D | N S' . . | n D P M | G R S . ||",
        "",
        "#voice harmony",
        "S . . . | G . . . | M . . . | P . . . ||",
        "",
        "#voice drone",
        "S,, . . . | . . . . | P,, . . . | . . . . ||"
      ],
      "id": "5141e785-3bbc-4065-86b8-e4458358a3ce"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 12. Advanced Composition - Sthayi & Antara",
        "",
        "A complete composition structure with multiple sections, combining all techniques."
      ],
      "id": "014fa0c4-8166-4f3b-ae63-880ec0ed5bfa"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tala Tintal(16)",
        "@tala_pattern dha dhin dhin dha | dha dhin dhin dha | dha tin tin ta | ta dhin dhin dha",
        "@tempo 100",
        "",
        "# Sthayi (First section)",
        "G M P D | N S' S' . | n D P M | G R S . ||",
        "G M P D | N S' R' S' | n D P M | G R S . ||",
        "",
        "# Antara (Second section)",
        "S' R' G' M' | P' D' N' S'' | n' D' P' M' | G' R' S' . ||"
      ],
      "id": "4c2a17d2-c980-4a4c-87c2-3f34a8408205"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 13. Complex Taans with Ornaments",
        "",
        "Fast passages (taans) combined with ornamentation for expressive performance."
      ],
      "id": "890d7294-6037-4511-bb64-33955cb7670f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tempo 120",
        "",
        "# Taan with meend",
        "S:0.5 R:0.5 G+meend(M):0.5 M:0.5 | P:0.5 D:0.5 N:0.5 S':0.5 ||",
        "",
        "# Taan with kan",
        "S+kan(N):0.5 R+kan(S):0.5 | G+kan(R):0.5 M+kan(G):0.5 | P+kan(M):0.5 D+kan(P):0.5 ||",
        "",
        "# Mixed ornamentation",
        "G+meend(P)+kan(M):1 | D+meend(N)+kampita(8):1 | S'+shake:1 . . . ||"
      ],
      "id": "d3dba197-537e-41dc-b71b-2eeda4b2d544"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 14. Tempo & Laya Variations",
        "",
        "Control speed with `@tempo` directive:",
        "- Lower tempo (60-80) = Vilambit (slow)",
        "- Medium tempo (100-120) = Madhya (medium)",
        "- Higher tempo (140+) = Drut (fast)"
      ],
      "id": "a538d337-8f38-4dcf-a0b1-e89e1175cbdb"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tempo 60",
        "",
        "# Vilambit (slow) - Alap style",
        "S . . . . . . . | R . . . . . . . | G . . . . . . . | M . . . . . . . ||"
      ],
      "id": "5dc2f9e4-9d8d-4ad0-893a-838051209e9a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tempo 140",
        "",
        "# Drut (fast) - Fast taan",
        "S:0.25 R:0.25 G:0.25 M:0.25 | P:0.25 D:0.25 N:0.25 S':0.25 |",
        "S':0.25 N:0.25 D:0.25 P:0.25 | M:0.25 G:0.25 R:0.25 S:0.25 ||"
      ],
      "id": "b4fc9e79-cc94-4df8-8e6b-e91a0c7b0370"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 15. Complete Raag Khamaj Performance",
        "",
        "A comprehensive example combining all elements: multiple voices, ornamentation, different sections, and expressive techniques."
      ],
      "id": "3a4b5f64-6562-4a35-b1d1-08baccc3d832"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "music",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "sargam-v1"
      },
      "source": [
        "@sa D4",
        "@tala Tintal(16)",
        "@tala_pattern dha dhin dhin dha | dha dhin dhin dha | dha tin tin ta | ta dhin dhin dha",
        "@tempo 100",
        "",
        "#voice melody",
        "G+kan(R) M+kan(G) P+meend(D) D | N+kan(D) S'+shake . . |",
        "n+meend(D) D P M+andolan(0.1) | G R+kan(S) S . . ||",
        "",
        "#voice tanpura",
        "S,, . . . | P,, . . . | S,, . . . | P,, . . . ||"
      ],
      "id": "9b85a377-b071-4baa-b27c-c5af080c9c5b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Summary",
        "",
        "This notebook has demonstrated all major features of the **sargam-v1** language:",
        "",
        "✅ **Basic Notation**: Swaras, variants (komal/tivra), octaves  ",
        "✅ **Timing**: Durations, rests, holds  ",
        "✅ **Rhythm**: Talas, bar markers, cycles  ",
        "✅ **Ornamentation**: Meend, kan, andolan, kampita, shake  ",
        "✅ **Microtones**: Shruti notation with cents/semitones  ",
        "✅ **Lyrics**: Text association with notes  ",
        "✅ **Polyphony**: Multiple voices playing simultaneously  ",
        "✅ **Tempo Control**: Vilambit, Madhya, Drut  ",
        "✅ **Complex Compositions**: Sthayi, Antara, Taans  ",
        "",
        "All while exploring the beautiful Raag Khamaj! 🎵"
      ],
      "id": "479c4ddf-f14a-4cb0-b872-e5676142a3a1"
    }
  ]
}